=== handler-side protocol: does call_runner block the kopf event loop? ===
controller image: jit-controller
kopf 1.44.6: event-loop thread 281473607140544; sync handler ran on thread 281473518268800; separate executor thread: True
code reading: jit-controller/main.py handle_deployment is a synchronous def (line 129) and
resync_referenced_by is a synchronous @kopf.timer def (line 816); provision_infra -> call_runner
(line 352) is a plain blocking requests.post with timeout=600.
kopf/_core/actions/invocation.py line 134 executes a synchronous handler with
loop.run_in_executor(executor, real_fn), i.e. on a worker thread, not the event loop.
call_runner blocking verdict: call_runner does not block the kopf event loop - kopf offloads
synchronous handlers to an executor thread, so the 30s resync keeps ticking while an apply runs;
asyncio.to_thread would be required only if S26 converts the handler to async def.

